      "id": 36681,
      "name": "awp832",
      "username": "awp832",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/a9a28c/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2012-08-25T01:14:52.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>No, because Hypersonic can hit Carrion Fields and Matriarch before dealing damage to the birds, thereby bypassing \"revenge\" damage, unlike Hairtrigger. &nbsp; Tach is certainly helpful vs matriarch, but any number of heroes including Wraith, Fixer, Haka, or Legacy can take her place and help deal with the Revenge damage.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Sometimes it depends on what the villain draw is. &nbsp; &nbsp;Any &nbsp;team of heroes that doesnt have Ongoing destruction can find themselves up the creek against Dawn or Plague Rat. &nbsp;Heroes that take a while to get rolling and those wihtout a damaging base power can be in a world of hurt vs Omnitron if he plays a first turn electropulse explosive.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Chariman does horrible things to any team, &nbsp; Matriarch in Rook City is particularly brutal. &nbsp;Omnitron on Mars is tough too. &nbsp; Zero, Bunker, Wraith, Expatriette on Mars vs any villain with any sort of equipment destruction on top of what Mars does can be very difficult.</p>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:10:33.530Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
